<title>SINGAPORE: Intraco expects difficult conditions.</title>
<headline>Intraco expects difficult conditions.</headline>
<dateline>SINAGPORE 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Diversified trading conglomerate Intraco Ltd said on Wednesday it expected current difficult operating conditions to continue, at least for the first half of 1997.  </p>
<p>The company said in a statement its automobile division was expected to have a difficult year with continued pressure on margins and sales volume.</p>
<p>It said Intraco expected a gradual improvement in the performance of its semiconductor business with the acquisition of new agencies in multimedia chips.</p>
<p>Intraco expected its food operations to improve with the establishment of a seafood distribution and marketing network.</p>
<p>Intraco's 1996 net profit fell 61.7 percent to Singapore $6.19 million from S$16.15 million.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703199)</p>
